  "description": "**As a** Site Merchandiser,\n\n**I want** to enable or disable the Environmental Qualities tab per locale in Business Manager,\n\n**so that** I can control which locales display EU compliance content on the PDP without requiring a code deployment.\n\n----\n\n**Background**\n\nThe PDP displays an Environmental Qualities tab on the EU storefront (SFCC-266). This tab should only render on specific locales (currently `en-FR` and `fr-FR`) and needs to be togglable by a merchandiser without a code deploy. This story covers the BM configuration layer only — rendering logic is covered in SFCC-266.\n\nTo be specific, this is about two site preferences in BM:\n\n  - **Show Environmental Qualities* (accepts one or more locales)\n  - **Default Environmental Qualities* (accepts a piece of text that will be the storefront’s default value if the product attribute is missing - and this can be translated)",
